  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "In a large mixing bowl, combine the egg yolks, whipping cream, low carb sweetener, and salt until the mixture is smooth.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "In a small mixing bowl, combine almond flour with baking powder; whisk it into the creamy egg mixture until uniform in appearance.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Using an electric mixer, beat the egg whites in a separate bowl until soft peaks form. Fold the egg whites into the batter.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Melt butter in a large non-stick frying pan over medium heat, then wipe with a paper towel to evenly distribute the butter for cooking. Spoon in the batter to make your pancakes; use about 2 tablespoons per pancake.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook for 3 minutes, or until lightly browned, and then gently flip each pancake and cook for an additional 2 minutes on the other side. Take care not to agitate the pancake before it's ready to flip or disaster will ensue.",
      "group": null
    },
